---
/**
 * **Sector workforce panel** — B2B 상품 지면. (seoulmarkets.com/data/sector-workforce-panel)
 *
 * ── 왜 지면인가 (사장님 지시 2026-08-08, 2번 38878) ──────────────
 *   「6번의 새 데이터가공 비즈니스를 위한 업무플로우를 초기부터 매출이 나게. 팔 수 있는 물건으로.」
 *   백년지도·임금패널과 같은 모양 — 파는 지면 + 「무엇이 들어 있나」 + 「곧 엽니다·알림 받기」.
 *   ⛔ 값(가격)은 지면에 넣지 않는다(사장님 확정 대기, 38376 규칙: 미정은 「곧 엽니다」로).
 *   ⛔ 결제는 붙이지 않는다 — 지금 필요한 것은 **살 뜻을 세는 칸**이다.
 *
 * ── 원본 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   판매정의 docs/상품안/6번-P1-판매정의.md · 업종체계 docs/SeoulMarkets-업종체계.md
 *   수치는 scripts/build-sector-panel.mjs 실측(시총 기준일 2026-08-05).
 *
 * ── 우리가 파는 것 ─────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   분류(공공 KSIC 유도)가 아니라, 그 위에 얹은 **우리 노동데이터**(근속·임금·성별·1인당 인건비).
 *   대형 벤더가 재무는 줘도 이건 안 준다. ⛔ GICS 데이터·상표는 쓰지 않는다.
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_URL } from '../../consts';

const TITLE = 'The sector workforce panel';
const SAMPLE = '2,644 listed companies · 11 sectors · market cap as of 2026-08-05';
const DESC =
  'Korean listed companies sorted into 11 standard sectors, each carrying the labour fingerprint the '
  + 'big vendors leave out: tenure, average pay, gender pay gap, female share and capital-per-head — '
  + 'with market leaders separated from the rest, for 2,644 companies.';

/** 섹터 요약 — build-sector-panel.mjs 실측(시총 20260805). 화면과 하나의 출처로 묶는다. */
const 섹터 = [
  ['Information Technology', '52.1%', '93%', '6.5y', '57.8m', '21%'],
  ['Industrials', '14.5%', '22%', '6.4y', '61.0m', '14%'],
  ['Financials', '13.4%', '35%', '6.2y', '115.8m', '35%'],
  ['Consumer Discretionary', '6.1%', '56%', '7.1y', '57.4m', '30%'],
  ['Health Care', '4.8%', '47%', '4.9y', '57.1m', '40%'],
  ['Materials', '3.9%', '30%', '8.6y', '61.6m', '13%'],
  ['Communication Services', '3.1%', '41%', '4.7y', '60.9m', '35%'],
];

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: 'Korean listed-company sector workforce panel',
  description: DESC,
  url: `${SITE_URL}/data/sector-workforce-panel`,
  temporalCoverage: '2026',
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'SeoulMarkets', url: SITE_URL },
  variableMeasured: [
    'average tenure', 'average annual pay', 'female-to-male pay ratio',
    'female share', 'market cap per employee', 'sector concentration',
  ],
};
---

<Base title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd} noAds>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="pp">
      <p class="kicker">SeoulMarkets · data for licence</p>
      <h1>The sector workforce panel</h1>
      <p class="sample">{SAMPLE}</p>
      <p class="lead">
        Every listed company files, once a year, how long its people stay, what it pays them, and how
        that splits by gender. Almost nobody joins it up. We sort all of Korea's listed companies into
        11 standard sectors and hand you the one thing the big data vendors leave out of their
        terminals: <b>the labour fingerprint of each sector</b> — tenure, pay, the gender gap, and how
        concentrated the market cap really is.
      </p>

      <!-- 다섯 줄 요약 -->
      <ol class="five">
        <li><b>What it is</b> — 2,644 listed companies in 11 sectors, each row carrying tenure, average
          pay, gender pay gap, female share and market-cap-per-employee, with sector leaders flagged.</li>
        <li><b>Why trust it</b> — every figure is re-derived from the company's own annual filing
          (DART) and the exchange's close, and re-checked. Discrepancies are logged, not hidden.</li>
        <li><b>How big</b> — 2,862 listed companies mapped, 2,644 joined to a market cap. Not a
          sample — the whole board.</li>
        <li><b>What only we have</b> — the big vendors sell price and financials. Tenure, churn,
          gender pay gap and pay-per-head by sector are the columns they don't carry.</li>
        <li><b>The form</b> — one CSV per sector, plus an all-sector summary. Leaders vs the rest on
          every row. Refreshed quarterly, on the filing cycle.</li>
      </ol>

      <!-- ① 무엇을 재나 -->
      <section class="blk">
        <h2>① The labour fingerprint — by sector</h2>
        <p>
          Each sector reads differently, and the difference is the product. IT is more than half the
          market's value and brutally concentrated; finance pays the most; health care is the youngest
          and most female. Median figures shown — the CSV carries every company.
        </p>
        <table class="press">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Sector</th><th class="r">Mkt weight</th><th class="r">Top-3 conc.</th>
              <th class="r">Tenure</th><th class="r">Pay (median)</th><th class="r">Female</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {섹터.map((s) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="axis">{s[0]}</td>
                <td class="r">{s[1]}</td><td class="r">{s[2]}</td>
                <td class="r">{s[3]}</td><td class="r">₩{s[4]}</td><td class="r">{s[5]}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="fine">
          Read IT's 93%: the three biggest names hold 93% of the sector's market cap. A buyer weighing
          "Korean tech" is really weighing three companies — that is exactly what a concentration
          column tells you and a price feed does not.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- ② 무엇이 들어 있나 -->
      <section class="blk">
        <h2>② What you get</h2>
        <table class="kv">
          <tbody>
            <tr><th>Files</th><td colspan="2">One CSV per sector plus an all-sector summary. Columns:
              sector · source industry (KSIC) · company · ticker · <b>leader / other</b> · market cap ·
              employees · average annual pay · average tenure · gender pay ratio · female share ·
              market-cap-per-employee.</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Leaders vs the rest</th><td colspan="2">Every row is flagged <b>leader</b> or{' '}
              <b>other</b> by market-cap weight, so you can read a sector as its handful of movers plus
              a long tail — not one undifferentiated list.</td></tr>
            <tr><th>The sector map</th><td colspan="2">Our own 11-sector scheme, derived from public
              KSIC. <b>No GICS data or trademark is used or resold</b> — redistribution-free.</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Definitions</th><td colspan="2">A <code>method.md</code> quoting each field from
              the source filing, plus a <code>corrections.csv</code> — every figure we changed after
              first publishing it, never a silent edit.</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Refresh</th><td colspan="2">Quarterly, on the DART filing cycle.</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Source</th><td colspan="2">DART annual reports (employment & pay) and KRX close via
              data.go.kr, licence "unrestricted". What we sell is our parse, join and correction
              record — not the raw filings.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <!-- ③ 왜 우리 것인가 -->
      <section class="blk">
        <h2>③ Why this is ours to sell — and no one else's</h2>
        <ul class="arrows">
          <li><b>The columns are the moat.</b> Price and financials are everywhere. Tenure, churn,
            gender pay gap and pay-per-head, joined to a sector map, are not sold anywhere in Korea.</li>
          <li><b>Built from filings, not surveys.</b> Every number comes from a company's own legal
            disclosure — auditable, cite-able, and it reconciles to the source.</li>
          <li><b>We carry our own corrections.</b> A dataset that logs what it changed is worth more
            than one that hides it. We sell trust, so the correction record ships with the data.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="cta">
        <h2>Ask for the panel</h2>
        <p class="cta__lead">
          Want a sample sector cut or the full 11-sector panel for your desk? Leave a work email and we
          send the sample and the current licensing terms. It reaches us directly — no account, and
          this is not the newsletter.
        </p>
        {
          /* 사는 길. 죽은 mailto 대신 실제로 도는 /v1/subscribe 로 접수한다. source='sector-panel'
             로 이 상품 문의를 뉴스레터·임금패널과 갈라 센다.
             (JSX 주석이라 지면으로 나가지 않는다) */
        }
        <form class="ask" method="post" action="/v1/subscribe" data-source="sector-panel">
          <label class="vh" for="ask-email">Work email</label>
          <div class="ask__row">
            <input
              id="ask-email"
              type="email"
              name="email"
              required
              autocomplete="email"
              inputmode="email"
              placeholder="you@company.com"
              aria-describedby="ask-note"
            />
            <button type="submit">Request the panel</button>
          </div>
          <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
            <label for="ask-hp">Leave this field empty</label>
            <input id="ask-hp" type="text" name="hp" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
          </div>
          <p class="ask__note" id="ask-note">We store your address and that you asked about the sector
            panel. We never sell or share it.</p>
          <p class="ask__msg" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </form>
        <p class="cta__also">
          While you are here, the company-level table this is built from is free —{' '}
          <a href="/data/korean-listed-workforce.csv" download>the whole listed-company table (CSV)</a>,
          or browse it on the <a href="/rankings">rankings page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="fine bottom">
        Market cap as of 2026-08-05 (KRX via data.go.kr) · Employment & pay from DART annual filings ·
        Sector map derived from public KSIC, no GICS data used · Not investment advice.
        Browse <a href="/data">all SeoulMarkets datasets</a>. See our <a href="/terms">terms of use</a> and <a href="/refund">refund policy</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    (() => {
      const form = document.querySelector('form.ask');
      if (!form) return;
      const input = form.querySelector('input[name="email"]');
      const hp = form.querySelector('input[name="hp"]');
      const btn = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');
      const msg = form.querySelector('.ask__msg');
      const say = (state, text) => { msg.dataset.state = state; msg.textContent = text; };
      form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
        e.preventDefault();
        const email = input.value.trim();
        if (!email) return;
        btn.disabled = true;
        const was = btn.textContent;
        btn.textContent = 'Sending…';
        delete msg.dataset.state;
        try {
          const res = await fetch('/v1/subscribe', {
            method: 'POST',
            headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({ email, hp: hp.value, source: form.dataset.source || 'sector-panel' }),
          });
          const data = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));
          if (res.ok && data.ok) {
            say('ok', 'Thanks — we have your address and will email you the sample and the terms.');
            form.reset();
          } else {
            say('error', data?.error?.message || data?.message || 'Could not send. Please try again.');
          }
        } catch {
          say('error', 'Network error. Please try again.');
        } finally {
          btn.disabled = false;
          btn.textContent = was;
        }
      });
    })();
  </script>
</Base>

<style>
  .pp { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  .kicker { font-size: .74rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--accent);
            font-weight: 700; margin: 1.2rem 0 .3rem; }
  .pp h1 { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 5vw, 2.4rem); line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 .5rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .pp .sample { font-size: .9rem; color: var(--muted); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
                margin: 0 0 1.4rem; padding-bottom: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .pp .lead { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 1.8rem; }
  .pp .lead b { font-weight: 650; }

  .five { margin: 0 0 2.4rem; padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem 1.1rem 2.4rem; background: var(--card);
          border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; }
  .five li { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: .92rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .five li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .five li b { color: var(--ink); }

  .blk { margin: 0 0 2.2rem; }
  .blk h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0 0 .8rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .blk p { line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 .8rem; }

  table.kv, table.press { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .9rem; margin: 0 0 .8rem; }
  table.kv th, table.kv td, table.press th, table.press td {
    padding: .55rem .6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  table.kv th { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); white-space: nowrap; width: 1%; }
  table.kv td { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  table.kv td.note { color: var(--muted); font-size: .82rem; white-space: normal;
                     font-variant-numeric: normal; }
  table.kv td[colspan] { white-space: normal; line-height: 1.6; }
  table.press th { font-size: .74rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em;
                   color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
  table.press td.axis { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); vertical-align: middle;
                        white-space: nowrap; }
  .r { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }

  .arrows { padding-left: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 .8rem; }
  .arrows li { margin: 0 0 .5rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .arrows li b { color: var(--ink); }

  code { font-family: var(--mono, ui-monospace, monospace); font-size: .86em;
         background: var(--card); padding: .1em .35em; border-radius: 4px; }

  .cta { margin: 2.4rem 0 0; padding: 1.3rem 1.3rem; border: 1px solid var(--line);
         border-radius: 10px; background: var(--card); }
  .cta h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
  .cta p { line-height: 1.7; font-size: .95rem; }
  .cta__lead { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .cta__also { margin: 1.1rem 0 0; font-size: .88rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .cta a, .pp a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none;
                  border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor; padding-bottom: 1px; }
  .cta a:hover, .pp a:hover { color: var(--ink); }

  .vh { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden;
        clip: rect(0 0 0 0); clip-path: inset(50%); white-space: nowrap; }
  .ask__row { display: flex; gap: .5rem; max-width: 30rem; }
  .ask__row input { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; font: inherit; font-size: .95rem; padding: .6rem .7rem;
    color: var(--ink); background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; }
  .ask__row input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 1px; border-color: var(--accent); }
  .ask__row button { flex: 0 0 auto; font: inherit; font-size: .92rem; font-weight: 650; cursor: pointer;
    padding: .6rem 1rem; color: var(--bg); background: var(--ink); border: 1px solid var(--ink); border-radius: 6px; }
  .ask__row button:hover { opacity: .9; }
  .ask__row button[disabled] { opacity: .6; cursor: default; }
  .hp { position: absolute; left: -9999px; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; }
  .ask__note { margin: .6rem 0 0; font-size: .8rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.55; }
  .ask__msg { margin: .6rem 0 0; font-size: .88rem; line-height: 1.55; display: none; }
  .ask__msg[data-state] { display: block; }
  .ask__msg[data-state='ok'] { color: var(--up, #1a7f37); }
  .ask__msg[data-state='error'] { color: var(--down, #c0392b); }
  @media (max-width: 30rem) { .ask__row { flex-direction: column; } .ask__row button { width: 100%; } }

  .fine { font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; }
  .fine.bottom { margin: 2.4rem 0 1rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    table.kv th { white-space: normal; }
    .pp .sample { white-space: normal; }
  }
</style>
